    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1950-p24.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Isolating and squaring gives \\[ \\begin{aligned} \\sqrt{x-2}&=4-x,\\\\ x-2&=(4-x)^2,\\\\ x^2-9x+18&=0. \\end{aligned} \\] The quadratic roots are \\(3\\) and \\(6.\\) The value \\(3\\) satisfies the original equation, but \\(6\\) gives \\(6+\\sqrt4=8,\\) so it is extraneous.\n\nThus, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Isolate the square root before squaring",
        "Check every root of the resulting quadratic in the original equation"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
